From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Mar 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: pn553: Add 100ms delay after VEN assertion

The NXP PN553 chip needs time to boot after VEN goes high. Without
this delay, the HAL's first I2C transaction arrives within ~1ms and
gets NACKed by the chip.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific]
---
 drivers/nfc/pn553-i2c/pn553.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/nfc/pn553-i2c/pn553.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/pn553-i2c/pn553.c
@@ -528,6 +528,7 @@
             pn544_dev->nfc_ven_enabled = true;
             if (pn544_dev->spi_ven_enabled == false || (pn544_dev->chip_pwr_scheme == PN80T_EXT_PMU_SCHEME)) {
                 gpio_set_value(pn544_dev->ven_gpio, 1);
+                msleep(100); /* Wait for NFC chip to boot after VEN high */
             }
         } else if (arg == 0) {
             /* power off */
